      "flags": [
        {
          "id": "f1",
          "kind": "issue",
          "title": "update_data destroys and rebuilds every widget on each 2s poll while hovering",
          "note": "update_data (line 1191) starts with `for child in self.inner.get_children(): self.inner.remove(child)` then reconstructs every label, bar and separator, ending in show_all(). Because _apply_data calls it on every poll while the panel is visible, the whole panel is torn down and rebuilt 30x/min during hover. It works today because the tree is small (~15 widgets), but multi-GPU multiplies that per card, and rebuilding is why any future interactive control in the panel (a per-GPU expander, a selected row) cannot hold state across a poll.",
          "fix": "Build the row widgets once in __init__ and have update_data only set label text / bar fractions. If the device count changes, rebuild just the GPU section rather than the whole panel.",
          "by": "agent",
          "at": "2026-08-31T19:36:49.879Z"
        }
      ],
