      "flags": [
        {
          "id": "f1",
          "kind": "idea",
          "title": "Temp/power/fan are unavailable for remote endpoints — no rows at all when --host is another machine",
          "note": "ComfyUI's /system_stats exposes VRAM only (verified: device keys are name/type/index/vram_total/vram_free/torch_vram_total/torch_vram_free — no temperature, power, utilisation or fan). So telemetry has to come from the machine itself, and _endpoint_is_local() gates it off whenever --host points elsewhere. Correct — showing this box's sensors beside a remote server's VRAM would silently describe two machines — but it means the README's remote/NAS use case gets VRAM only, with no hint as to why the CPU and temperature rows vanished.",
          "fix": "If remote telemetry is wanted: either run a tiny agent on the ComfyUI host exposing nvidia-smi over HTTP, or use a ComfyUI extension that adds temps to the API (e.g. Crystools), and have the widget prefer server-provided sensor fields when present, falling back to local. Cheaper interim: render a dim \"sensors: local only\" note in the panel when the endpoint is remote.",
          "by": "agent",
          "at": "2026-08-31T19:49:07.732Z"
        }
      ]
    },
